---
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import Banner from "../../components/Banner.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

type TeamMember = { image: ImageMetadata; name: string; role?: string };

import Alexis from "../../images/team/alexis-jacomy.jpg";
import Benoit from "../../images/team/benoit-simard.jpeg";
import Clement from "../../images/team/clement-levallois.png";
import Eduardo from "../../images/team/eduardo-ramos-ibanez.png";
import Martin from "../../images/team/martin-grandjean.png";
import MathieuB from "../../images/team/mathieu-bastian.png";
import MathieuJ from "../../images/team/mathieu-jacomy.png";
import Matthieu from "../../images/team/matthieu-totet.png";
import Nicolas from "../../images/team/nicolas-bouchaib.jpeg";
import Paul from "../../images/team/paul-girard.jpeg";

const TEAM: TeamMember[] = [
  { image: MathieuJ, name: "Mathieu Jacomy", role: "Project management and design" },
  { image: MathieuB, name: "Mathieu Bastian", role: "Java architect" },
  { image: Eduardo, name: "Eduardo Ramos Ibáñez", role: "Java lead developer" },
  { image: Matthieu, name: "Matthieu Totet", role: "Java codebase and plugins" },
  { image: Paul, name: "Paul Girard", role: "Gephi Lite team" },
  { image: Alexis, name: "Alexis jacomy", role: "Gephi Lite team" },
  { image: Benoit, name: "Benoit Simard", role: "Gephi Lite team" },
  { image: Martin, name: "Martin Grandjean", role: "Community management" },
  { image: Clement, name: "Clément Levallois", role: "Community emulation" },
  { image: Nicolas, name: "Nicolas Bouchaïb", role: "Community emulation" },
];
---

<Layout pageId="about">
  <Banner>
    <h1>About Gephi</h1>
  </Banner>

  <main class="py-5">
    <section class="feature-container pb-5">
      <section class="feature feature-left feature-flat py-4" id="history">
        <section class="feature-headline">
          <div class="feature-text">
            <h2>
              <Icon name="ph:cake" class="text-primary" />
              <span>Project history</span>
            </h2>
            <p>
              Gephi has been initially developed by students of the <a href="https://www.utc.fr/en/"
                >University of Technology of Compiègne</a
              >, in France. It has been selected for the <a href="https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/"
                >Google Summer of Code</a
              > from 2009 to 2013. It received the <a
                href="https://gephi.wordpress.com/2010/09/29/gephi-at-javaone-2010/">Duke's Choice Award</a
              > at JavaOne 2010 and the <a
                href="https://gephi.wordpress.com/2019/06/12/the-gephi-paper-gets-the-icwsm-test-of-time-award/"
                >Test of Time Award</a
              > at ICWSM 2019.
            </p>
            <p>
              After a less active period of development, the <a href="/community#gephi-weeks">Gephi team gathers</a>
              every year since 2021 to maintain the codebase, meets users, discuss and design new features.
            </p>
            <p>
              During Gephi Week 2022, we decided to create a new product in the Gephi community called <a href="/lite"
                >Gephi Lite</a
              >, a web version of Gephi.
            </p>
            <p>
              For more information about the evolution of the project, check our <a href="https://gephi.wordpress.com"
                >blog</a
              >.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section class="feature feature-left feature-flat py-4" id="roadmap">
        <section class="feature-headline">
          <div class="feature-text">
            <h2>
              <Icon name="ph:scales" class="text-primary" />
              <span>Project governance</span>
            </h2>

            <p>
              The Gephi community organized itself around the Gephi committee which gathers top contributors. The
              committee is responsible for deciding how to use the ressources we have at end: free times and donations.
              The Gephi committee takes decisions through a lazy consensus model: the unanimity of members voicing their
              position, with a timeframe of at least two weeks for making their position known. In other words,
              committee members who decide to not take position in a given discussion consent to its outcome.
            </p>
            <p>
              The committee can decide to change those rules, and add or remove members of the committee. Changing rules
              and adding is decided using the lazy consensus described above. Removing a member is decided using the
              same lazy consensus rule minus that member. Each member must consent to participate, and can unilaterally
              leave the committee at any point.
            </p>
            <p>
              Our financial activities are organized under the umbrella of our fiscal host <a
                href="https://opencollective.com/gephi">Open Collective</a
              >. Donations are managed by their team and we decide how to use it in total transparent way. So far our
              main expenses are the organization of our yearly <a href="/community#gephi-weeks">Gephi Weeks</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section class="feature feature-left feature-flat py-4" id="roadmap">
        <section class="feature-headline">
          <div class="feature-text">
            <h2>
              <Icon name="ph:road-horizon" class="text-primary" />
              <span>Project roadmap</span>
            </h2>

            <p>
              Beyond the codebase, we also work on the project’s structure and other aspects. Next up we aim at this:
            </p>
            <ul class="fs-4 ps-md-0 mt-0">
              <li>
                <strong>Consolidate our community.</strong> More frequent communication with contributors and users about
                what we do and how everyone can take a role in our community.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Raise funds and facilitate donations.</strong> We need funds for the Gephi Weeks and ultimately, for
                recurrent contributors.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Recruit core contributors.</strong> Having developers familiar with the codebases is key to the sustainability
                of the project.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Gephi Weeks.</strong> We meet for an entire week every year, and that’s a great moment to care for
                and contribute to the project.
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              To learn more about the various ways to engage with the project, read our <a href="/community"
                >community page</a
              >.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section class="feature feature-left feature-flat py-4" id="committee">
        <section class="feature-headline">
          <div class="feature-text">
            <h2>
              <Icon name="ph:users-three" class="text-primary" />
              <span>The Gephi committee</span>
            </h2>
            <p>
              Our project is lead by a committee of top contributors which organizes the project. Here is the current
              list of committee members:
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="feature-text mw-100">
          <div class="team-members">
            {
              TEAM.map((member) => (
                <div class="team-member" style="width: 230px">
                  <Image
                    width="200"
                    height="200"
                    class="img-thumbnail"
                    layout="constrained"
                    src={member.image}
                    alt={`${member.name}'s picture`}
                  />
                  <h3 class="fs-5 mb-0">{member.name}</h3>
                  {member.role && <div class="text-muted">{member.role}</div>}
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="feature feature-left feature-flat py-4" id="contributors">
        <section class="feature-headline">
          <div class="feature-text">
            <h2>
              <Icon name="ph:users-four" class="text-primary" />
              <span>The Gephi contributors</span>
            </h2>
            <p>
              Gephi tools have been made possible by so many people that it's hard to name them all, from developers, to
              content creators, to translators, to issue reporters...
            </p>
            <p>
              We thank the following contributors, who have improved the code or added new features: Anna Kharitonova,
              Antonin Delpeuch, Côme Brocas, Sukankana Chakraborty, Walton Goga.
            </p>
            <p>
              Plugin developers meaningfully contribute to the communusers-fourity, and we want to thank all of their
              contributions. You can directly find plugin authors in <a href="desktop/plugins">Plugins</a>.
            </p>
            <p>
              The years Gephi participated in the Google Summer of Code was rich in collaboration and contributions. We
              thank mentors Eytan Adar, Christian Tominski, Cezary Bartosiak, Julian Bilcke, Antonio Patriarca and
              Eduardo Ramos Ibáñez. We also thank Helder Suzuki, Jeremy Subtil, Patrick McSweeney, André Panisson,
              Antonio Patriarca, Martin Škurla, Yi Du, Yudi Xue, Vojtech Bardiovsky, Ernesto Aneiros, Urban Škudnik,
              Keheliya Gallaba, Daniel Bernardes, Luiz Ribeiro, Min Wu, Vikash Anand, Taras Klaskovsky, Romain Yon,
              Eduardo Espinoza, Vijesh M. and Nitesh Bhargava for their student contributions.
            </p>
            <p>
              Gephi is a multilingual software thanks to its many translators. We are grateful for their work. You can
              find them directly on our <a href="https://hosted.weblate.org/projects/gephi/">Weblate</a>.
            </p>
            <p>
              Finally, we thank key early-days contributors and supporters Sébastien Heymann, Guillaume Lebourgeois,
              Dana Diminescu, Camille Maussang, Aurélien Beltrame, Stéphane Raux, Alain Le Berre, Guilhem Fouetillou and
              Franck Ghitalla.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
